---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import nickPhoto from '../assets/nick-noreña.jpeg';
---

<MarketingLayout
	title="About | People/Purpose/Product"
	description="People/Purpose/Product is an experimentation practice working with mission-driven teams to build products people actually use and figure out where AI fits in their work."
>
	<section class="page-header">
		<h1>About</h1>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section team-section">
		<h2>Nick Noreña</h2>
		<div class="person">
			<Image src={nickPhoto} alt="Nick Noreña" width={320} height={320} class="photo" />
			<div class="bio">
				<p class="role">Founder</p>
				<p>
					Nick has spent his career at the intersection of technology, organizations, and the people
					they serve. Before founding People/Purpose/Product, he spent years at Kromatic working with
					more than 30 organizations including Siemens, Unilever, General Mills, the US Government,
					and United Way, teaching innovation tools and helping teams build new capabilities.
				</p>
				<p>
					His background is in product management, entrepreneurship, and organizational change.
					He started in San Francisco's tech ecosystem as a founder, then spent years helping
					enterprise and mission-driven organizations understand what it means to build products
					that actually serve people.
				</p>
				<p>
					Now he's focused on a narrow question: what happens when mission-driven organizations
					get access to the same tools enterprises have, and use them without losing what makes
					them different?
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>Our collaborators</h2>
		<!-- Spike: unnamed by design, employed elsewhere full-time -->
		<p>
			People/Purpose/Product works with a small group of experienced collaborators on a
			project basis. Our team includes an AI engineer and product strategist with a background
			in enterprise software and AI systems, bringing technical depth to the problems that
			need it.
		</p>
		<p>
			We keep the team small deliberately. Every person on a project is someone whose
			judgment we trust.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>How we work</h2>
		<p>
			The model comes from places like Pivotal Labs and 37signals: build with clients, not for
			them. Every engagement is designed so that by the time it ends, your team understands what
			was built and why, and can maintain and extend it without coming back to us.
		</p>
		<p>
			We're not interested in dependency. We're interested in capability.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section closing">
		<a href="/work-with-us" class="cta-button">Work with us →</a>
	</section>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
	.page-header {
		padding: 3em 0 2.5em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		margin-bottom: 3em;
	}
	.page-header h1 {
		font-size: 3rem;
		line-height: 1.1;
	}

	.content-section {
		margin-bottom: 3em;
		padding-bottom: 3em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		max-width: 720px;
	}
	.content-section h2 {
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75em;
	}
	.closing {
		border-bottom: none;
	}

	/* Team layout */
	.person {
		display: flex;
		gap: 2em;
		align-items: flex-start;
	}
	.photo {
		width: 160px;
		height: 160px;
		min-width: 160px;
		border-radius: 8px;
		object-fit: cover;
	}
	.bio .role {
		font-weight: 700;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
		margin-bottom: 0.75em;
	}

	.cta-button {
		display: inline-block;
		background: var(--accent);
		color: white;
		padding: 0.75em 1.5em;
		border-radius: 4px;
		text-decoration: none;
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 1rem;
		transition: background 0.2s ease;
	}
	.cta-button:hover {
		background: var(--accent-dark);
		color: white;
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.page-header h1 {
			font-size: 2.25rem;
		}
		.person {
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 1.5em;
		}
		.photo {
			width: 120px;
			height: 120px;
			min-width: 120px;
		}
	}
</style>
